FFmpeg (full release package only)
----------------------------------

The full release package (avdbcms-X.Y.Z.zip) contains ready-built FFmpeg
programs in bin/. AVDBCMS runs them as separate programs. They are licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3, and their license and readme
files stay next to them:

Folder            What it holds                                   License file
bin/linux-x64/    ffmpeg, ffprobe: static build of FFmpeg 7.0.2   GPLv3.txt, readme.txt
                  (ffmpeg-7.0.2-amd64-static) by John Van Sickle,
                  https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/
bin/linux-arm64/  ffmpeg, ffprobe: static build of FFmpeg 7.0.2   GPLv3.txt, readme.txt
                  (ffmpeg-7.0.2-arm64-static) by John Van Sickle
bin/windows/      ffmpeg.exe, ffprobe.exe, ffplay.exe and the     LICENSE.txt
                  FFmpeg DLL files: FFmpeg build
                  N-124319-gb801f1fe6d-20260503 (git revision
                  b801f1fe6d), configured with --enable-gpl and
                  --enable-version3

The readme.txt files list the libraries built into the Linux programs and their
versions. Source code: the FFmpeg project publishes the source code of FFmpeg,
both release 7.0.2 and the git revision named above, at
https://ffmpeg.org/download.html. bin/README.md explains how AVDBCMS finds
these programs. The update package (avdbcms-update-X.Y.Z.zip) does not contain
bin/, and the source code repository holds only bin/README.md there.
